data.content:
Yes! MSTest v3.3+ introduced **generic `DynamicData`** attributes that work with tuples, eliminating the `object[]` casting:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[DynamicData<string, bool>(nameof(TestData))]
public void Validate_ReturnsExpected(string input, bool expected)
{
    var result = Validator.IsValid(input);
    Assert.AreEqual(expected, result);
}

public static IEnumerable<(string Input, bool Expected)> TestData =>
[
    ("valid@email.com", true),
    ("invalid", false),
    ("", false),
];
```

**What changed:**
- `[DynamicData<string, bool>(...)]` — generic type params enforce compile-time type safety between the data source and test method signature
- `IEnumerable<(string, bool)>` — value tuples instead of `object[]`, so no boxing/unboxing or runtime cast failures
- Named tuple elements (`Input`, `Expected`) improve readability in test explorer output

Generic overloads exist for up to 16 type parameters (`DynamicData<T1, ..., T16>`). Requires **MSTest 3.3+** (`Microsoft.Testing.Framework`).
